<!--
  Build dock, opened by any defense slot's build button: a compact pill that
  floats at one constant height above the clicked slot (BuildPanelSystem sets
  x from the slot, y/z fixed) and yaws to the camera via Billboard(lockY).
  The root is a transparent flex column: a small circular CLOSE button
  centered above a stadium-shaped bar — uniform border-radius = half the bar
  height rounds both side ends — holding one circular icon button per
  placeable unit, icon only: the overlaid live prices were removed (the
  wallet badge above already states the gold, and the glyph kept scattering
  under the digits). Icons are sized 4.5 — the largest the game-icons
  cannon glyph has ever rendered correctly inside the Ø10 circle. Uikit
  containers do not clip children (border-radius is not a mask), and past
  ~5 the cannon glyph scattered into fragments in every file variant
  tried — the original 512-unit path, a scale(0.046875) group wrapper, and
  a script-baked 0..24 path — while the mdi-family icons (recycle, bow:
  0..24 content) draw exactly even at 7. The dock keeps one shared icon
  size, so all three icons sit at the proven 4.5 with the cannon restored
  to its original cannon.svg. The top row centers one dark group — wallet badge and round close
  button side by side (same height 6 and radius, reading as a single
  segmented pill) — instead of pinning the badge to the rim; the badge is
  sized for "9999g", the worst-case wallet, so the digits never resize the
  group. Placement beside the close button rather than under the bar keeps
  the column's total height, and with it the clearance to the
  health bars below, unchanged. The bar is a left-aligned flex row
  and a native uikit scroll
  region (overflow: scroll, scrollbar hidden via scrollbar-width: 0): with
  more placeable units than fit, the extra circles drag in from the right.
  The bar is sized to two and a half button slots (padding 2 + 10 + gap 2 +
  10 + gap 2 + a half button 5 + padding 2 = 33): the tail stays empty while
  only two units exist, and a future third unit renders half-clipped at the
  right rim — the natural drag-me hint. Buttons use the <button> tag
  deliberately: <Panel> pulls the
  horizon kit's glass default (panelMaterialClass globally re-registered as
  GlassMaterial) and washes mid-gray class backgrounds out to white —
  Container (button) renders the class color exactly; the bar itself keeps
  panel-material-class: glass over #ffffffaa to match the pause-menu surface.
  A recycle button hangs centered below the bar: it sells the opening
  slot's live occupant for its depreciated book value (book value ×
  ECONOMY.replaceDiscount) and shares the unit
  buttons' visual language, but carries a red icon (#e5484d) so the income
  reads as a sale rather than a purchase. It dims (.dock-recycle-off) when
  the slot has no live occupant — nothing to sell — instead of hiding, so
  the column's outline stays constant across open/close cycles and the
  sell capability stays discoverable. The row deliberately grows the dock
  downward into the health-bar band (anchor and bar stay put); the dock's
  render-order 18 already outranks the bars (8/9), so it stays in front.
  BuildPanelSystem binds the clicks and drives a three-state
  class per unit button: .dock-unit (default), .dock-unit-off (its price
  above the current wallet — dimmed; the number itself is not shown) and
  .dock-unit-hidden (that unit already
  occupies the opening slot) — and rewrites the wallet badge every frame
  while the dock is open, so gold spent or earned elsewhere shows live.
  Runtime setProperties display would lose to the class layer, so every
  state change must be class-driven. Icons load through the <svg> tag's src
  (uikit Svg component: SVGLoader vector meshes, MeshBasicMaterial,
  tone-mapped off): cannon from the game-icons set, bow from boxicons; fills
  hardcoded #f2f4f7 because currentColor resolves to black in SVGLoader, and
  src resolves against the page base URL (not the .uikitml location), hence
  the ui/ prefix. Every non-colored container declares background-color
  #00000000: uikit containers default to an opaque white surface. Labels
  stay Latin — the bundled font atlas has no CJK glyph coverage. Dock
  palette: mid-gray #5d646d circles; dark
  gray #3a3f46 close button, matching the
  retired list rows. render-order 18
  keeps the dock under the menu button (20) and above the world overlays
  (health bars 8/9, hit flash 10).
-->
<style>
  .build-dock {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.5;
    width: 33;
    height: 32;
    render-order: 18;
    background-color: #00000000;
  }

  .dock-top {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 2;
    width: 33;
    height: 6;
    background-color: #00000000;
  }

  .wallet-badge {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    width: 12;
    height: 6;
    background-color: #3a3f46;
    border-radius: 3;
  }

  .wallet-text {
    display: flex;
    color: #ffd977;
    font-size: 2.8;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-align: center;
    background-color: #00000000;
  }

  .dock-close {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    width: 6;
    height: 6;
    background-color: #3a3f46;
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: 3.5;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-align: center;
    border-radius: 3;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .dock-close:hover {
    background-color: #464c55;
  }

  .dock-bar {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: flex-start;
    gap: 2;
    width: 33;
    height: 13;
    padding-left: 2;
    padding-right: 2;
    overflow: scroll;
    scrollbar-width: 0;
    border-radius: 6.5;
    panel-material-class: glass;
    background-color: #ffffffaa;
  }

  .dock-unit {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    width: 10;
    height: 10;
    background-color: #5d646d;
    border-radius: 5;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .dock-unit:hover {
    background-color: #6a717a;
  }

  .dock-unit:active {
    background-color: #515861;
  }

  .dock-unit-off {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    width: 10;
    height: 10;
    background-color: #41464d;
    border-radius: 5;
  }

  .dock-unit-hidden {
    display: none;
  }

  .dock-recycle {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    width: 10;
    height: 10;
    background-color: #5d646d;
    border-radius: 5;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .dock-recycle:hover {
    background-color: #6a717a;
  }

  .dock-recycle:active {
    background-color: #515861;
  }

  .dock-recycle-off {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    width: 10;
    height: 10;
    background-color: #41464d;
    border-radius: 5;
  }

  .unit-icon {
    display: flex;
    width: 4.5;
    height: 4.5;
    background-color: #00000000;
  }
</style>

<Panel class="build-dock">
  <Panel class="dock-top">
    <button class="wallet-badge">
      <Panel id="wallet-value" class="wallet-text">0g</Panel>
    </button>
    <button id="build-dismiss" class="dock-close">X</button>
  </Panel>
  <Panel class="dock-bar">
    <button id="row-cannon" class="dock-unit">
      <svg class="unit-icon" src="ui/icons/cannon.svg" ></svg>
    </button>
    <button id="row-sky-ballista" class="dock-unit">
      <svg class="unit-icon" src="ui/icons/bow-filled.svg" ></svg>
    </button>
  </Panel>
  <button id="dock-recycle" class="dock-recycle">
    <svg class="unit-icon" src="ui/icons/recycle.svg" ></svg>
  </button>
</Panel>
